Most items reduce to a few checks: whether two propositions can share a winner or runner-up, whether a qualifier must have at least 1 point, and the seed rules (one seed per group, no team seeded in two groups). Where a phrase could be read two ways, I took these readings:

- "Top N points" means exceeding N, so at least N+1.
- "Is it untrue that X" means the event is X, so a Yes or No label flips it accordingly.
- "Passed over for the seed" means not the seed.
- "Pot-one status" means being the group seed.

Two judgment calls worth noting. In the group items where the outcomes form a chain on only some pairs (H067, H078), I answered `none`, since the kind options cover only counting constraints and full chains. In H066 the feasible counts are only 1 or 3, which I reported as `at_least_k` with lower 1.

